# ASUS ROG Zephyrus G16 GA605KM: the FocalTech ASUF1209 touchpad (I2C
# 2808:0219). Its HID-BPF fixup (0010-FocalTech__ASUF1209.bpf.o) publishes
# each contact's width and height in sensor cells (0-15) as
# ABS_MT_TOUCH_MAJOR/MINOR and its signal strength (0-255) as ABS_MT_PRESSURE.
#
# Palms are told by strength. Captured on the G16, a fingertip reads at most
# 62 (resting, moving or clicking). Every palm that stays down more than a few
# reports goes past 70, most within a few frames and many up to 255; the
# lightest, resting just inside the right edge without the pad's palm flag,
# peak at 71-77. A deliberately flattened finger reaches 73, so at 70 it
# counts as a palm: the price of catching those light palms. Replayed through
# hid-multitouch and libinput, every palm-made scroll in the capture stopped
# at any threshold from 70 to 100 (130 let one back), and 70 let the least
# palm pointer motion through. A touch above it is a palm until it lifts.
# tests/channel/g16-touchpad-palm.sh checks this threshold against every
# contact of that capture (tests/channel/fixtures/asuf1209-touchpad-contacts.tsv).
#
# Size is no palm signal on this pad: the cell counts grow with motion (a
# fast swipe finger reads 9 x 7), and in the same replay a size threshold of
# 6 cells dropped a deliberate two-finger scroll while 7 and up let palm
# scrolls through. So no AttrPalmSizeThreshold.
#
# The strength is no touch-down signal either (a light fingertip reads about
# 20): pressure-based touch detection stays off, as it is without the fixup.
[ASUS ROG Zephyrus G16 GA605KM ASUF1209 touchpad]
MatchBus=i2c
MatchVendor=0x2808
MatchProduct=0x0219
MatchUdevType=touchpad
AttrPressureRange=none
AttrPalmPressureThreshold=70
